      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Please address the inline comments regarding DFU state/timeout handling, unused includes, magic response offsets, and unit test coverage.\n\n### Review Summary\n\n- **Functionality:** ❌ `dfu_poll_idle()` treats all unhandled `bState` values in `default:` as transient busy states (causing a 60s hang if the device is in `appIDLE`, `appDETACH`, `dfuUPLOAD-IDLE`, or an invalid state), does not check for non-zero `bStatus` outside `kDfuStateDfuError`, and multiplies the 24-bit `poll_timeout` by `1000` in signed `int` without clamping to the remaining timeout (`timeout - slept`), which can overflow `int` or sleep far beyond `kUsbDfuTimeoutMs`.\n- **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ❌ `dfu_poll_idle()` and `dfu_clear_status()` are added as uncalled `private` methods directly coupled to `libusb_*` and `usleep` in an uncompiled translation unit. Introducing a small virtual or injectable USB transport seam (matching sibling utilities in `util/egis/`, `util/focaltech/`, and `util/elan/`) allows compiling and unit-testing the DFU state machine in this CL.\n- **Code Simplicity:** ❌ Remove the unused `#include \u003cvector\u003e` (and include `\u003calgorithm\u003e` and `\u003ccstddef\u003e` for `std::min` and `size_t`), and move `delay_ms` after `switch (bState)` so it is only computed on the retry path.\n- **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ❌ Replace the raw positional indices `response[0]`..`response[4]` and fallback literal `1` in `dfu_poll_idle()` with named constants (`kDfuStatusOff`, `kDfuPollTimeoutOff`, `kDfuStateOff`, `kDfuMinPollDelayMs`), consistent with `kDfuDescTypeOff` and `kDfuDescXferSizeOff`.\n- **Security:** ✅ No security vulnerabilities identified.\n- **Testing:** ❌ No automated unit tests are included (`TEST\u003dNo standalone binary yet...`). Please add GoogleTest unit tests wired into `utils-test` in `util/build.mk` covering terminal states, transient busy states, `bwPollTimeout` boundaries, timeout boundaries, error/short-read paths, and `dfu_clear_status()`.\n- **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** ✅ `Size: M (+124, -0)`. Focused on a single logical change adding DFU status polling and clearing helpers to `RtsUsbDevice`.\n- **Commit Message:** ✅ Clear subject and concise prose rationale; please update `TEST\u003d` once unit tests are wired in.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/3e9f23d2-ae95-43fd-9a93-225bf455e097)",
