      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] `dfu_poll_idle()` has a few state-machine, timeout/overflow, and magic-offset issues:\n\n1. **Unchecked non-busy states and `bStatus` errors:** The `default:` branch in `switch (bState)` treats every state other than `kDfuStateDfuIdle` (`2`), `kDfuStateDfuDnloadIdle` (`5`), `kDfuStateDfuManifestWaitReset` (`8`), and `kDfuStateDfuError` (`10`) as a transient busy state. If the device is in `appIDLE` (`0`), `appDETACH` (`1`), `dfuUPLOAD-IDLE` (`9`), or an invalid state—or returns a non-zero `bStatus` before transitioning to `dfuERROR`—`dfu_poll_idle()` will spin for the full 60-second timeout instead of failing immediately. Explicitly handle the four DFU busy states (`dfuDNLOAD-SYNC \u003d 3`, `dfuDNBUSY \u003d 4`, `dfuMANIFEST-SYNC \u003d 6`, `dfuMANIFEST \u003d 7`) and fail immediately in `default:` or when `bStatus !\u003d kDfuStatusOk`.\n2. **24-bit `bwPollTimeout` multiplication overflow and oversleeping `kUsbDfuTimeoutMs`:** `poll_timeout` is a 24-bit unsigned integer up to `0xFFFFFF` (`16,777,215` ms). Computing `delay_ms * 1000` in signed `int` overflows when `poll_timeout \u003e 2,147,483` ms (undefined behavior), and sleeping for an unclamped `poll_timeout` allows a single poll iteration to block far past `kUsbDfuTimeoutMs`. Clamp `delay_ms` to `timeout - slept` and move its declaration after `switch (bState)` so it is only computed on the retry path.\n3. **Magic buffer offsets and fallback delay literal:** Replace raw positional indices `response[0]`..`response[4]` and the bare fallback literal `1` with named constants (`kDfuStatusOff`, `kDfuPollTimeoutOff`, `kDfuStateOff`, `kDfuMinPollDelayMs`), matching the descriptor offset constants at **lines 48–50**.\n\nSuggested replacement for **lines 36–43** and `dfu_poll_idle()`:\n\n```cpp\n/* DFU_GETSTATUS response: bStatus, bwPollTimeout[3], bState, iString */\nconstexpr size_t kDfuGetStatusResponseLen \u003d 6;\nconstexpr size_t kDfuStatusOff \u003d 0;\nconstexpr size_t kDfuPollTimeoutOff \u003d 1;\nconstexpr size_t kDfuStateOff \u003d 4;\n\n/* DFU status codes (from USB DFU spec) */\nconstexpr uint8_t kDfuStatusOk \u003d 0x00;\n\n/* DFU states (from USB DFU spec) */\nconstexpr uint8_t kDfuStateDfuIdle \u003d 2;\nconstexpr uint8_t kDfuStateDfuDnloadSync \u003d 3;\nconstexpr uint8_t kDfuStateDfuDnloadBusy \u003d 4;\nconstexpr uint8_t kDfuStateDfuDnloadIdle \u003d 5;\nconstexpr uint8_t kDfuStateDfuManifestSync \u003d 6;\nconstexpr uint8_t kDfuStateDfuManifest \u003d 7;\nconstexpr uint8_t kDfuStateDfuManifestWaitReset \u003d 8;\nconstexpr uint8_t kDfuStateDfuError \u003d 10;\n```\n\n```cpp\nbool RtsUsbDevice::dfu_poll_idle()\n{\n\tconstexpr int kDfuMinPollDelayMs \u003d 1;\n\tconstexpr useconds_t kUsPerMs \u003d 1000;\n\n\t/*\n\t * Use a generous timeout (60 s) for the overall polling, since the\n\t * manifest phase (flash programming) can take tens of seconds.\n\t */\n\tint timeout \u003d kUsbDfuTimeoutMs;\n\tint slept \u003d 0;\n\n\twhile (slept \u003c timeout) {\n\t\t/*\n\t\t * bmRequestType \u003d 0xA1: Device-to-Host, Class, Interface\n\t\t * bRequest \u003d kDfuGetStatus (0x03)\n\t\t * Data (6 bytes): bStatus, bwPollTimeout[3], bState, iString\n\t\t */\n\t\tuint8_t response[kDfuGetStatusResponseLen];\n\t\tint ret \u003d libusb_control_transfer(\n\t\t\tdev_handle_, kBmReqD2hClsIf, kDfuGetStatus, 0,\n\t\t\tstatic_cast\u003cuint16_t\u003e(dfu_interface_), response,\n\t\t\tsizeof(response), kUsbDfuTimeoutMs);\n\n\t\tif (ret \u003c static_cast\u003cint\u003e(kDfuGetStatusResponseLen)) {\n\t\t\tfprintf(stderr, \"DFU_GETSTATUS failed: %s\\n\",\n\t\t\t\tret \u003c 0 ? libusb_error_name(ret) : \"short read\");\n\t\t\treturn false;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tuint8_t bStatus \u003d response[kDfuStatusOff];\n\t\tuint32_t poll_timeout \u003d\n\t\t\tresponse[kDfuPollTimeoutOff] |\n\t\t\t(static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(response[kDfuPollTimeoutOff + 1])\n\t\t\t \u003c\u003c 8) |\n\t\t\t(static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(response[kDfuPollTimeoutOff + 2])\n\t\t\t \u003c\u003c 16);\n\t\tuint8_t bState \u003d response[kDfuStateOff];\n\n\t\tif (bStatus !\u003d kDfuStatusOk || bState \u003d\u003d kDfuStateDfuError) {\n\t\t\tfprintf(stderr, \"DFU error: bStatus\u003d%d, bState\u003d%d\\n\",\n\t\t\t\tbStatus, bState);\n\t\t\treturn false;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tswitch (bState) {\n\t\tcase kDfuStateDfuIdle:\n\t\tcase kDfuStateDfuDnloadIdle:\n\t\t\t/* Terminal success states. */\n\t\t\treturn true;\n\n\t\tcase kDfuStateDfuManifestWaitReset:\n\t\t\t/*\n\t\t\t * Device completed manifest and requests a USB reset.\n\t\t\t * Try issuing one; this may invalidate the device\n\t\t\t * handle (if the device re-enumerates), which is OK.\n\t\t\t */\n\t\t\tprintf(\"Device requests USB reset after manifest.\\n\");\n\t\t\tlibusb_reset_device(dev_handle_);\n\t\t\treturn true;\n\n\t\tcase kDfuStateDfuDnloadSync:\n\t\tcase kDfuStateDfuDnloadBusy:\n\t\tcase kDfuStateDfuManifestSync:\n\t\tcase kDfuStateDfuManifest:\n\t\t\t/*\n\t\t\t * Transient / busy states: sleep for the suggested\n\t\t\t * poll interval and retry.\n\t\t\t */\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\tfprintf(stderr, \"Unexpected DFU state: bState\u003d%d\\n\",\n\t\t\t\tbState);\n\t\t\treturn false;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tint remaining_ms \u003d timeout - slept;\n\t\tint delay_ms \u003d (poll_timeout \u003e 0) ?\n\t\t\t\t       static_cast\u003cint\u003e(std::min\u003cuint32_t\u003e(\n\t\t\t\t\t       poll_timeout, remaining_ms)) :\n\t\t\t\t       std::min(kDfuMinPollDelayMs,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tremaining_ms);\n\n\t\tusleep(static_cast\u003cuseconds_t\u003e(delay_ms) * kUsPerMs);\n\t\tslept +\u003d delay_ms;\n\t}\n\n\tfprintf(stderr, \"Timed out waiting for DFU idle state.\\n\");\n\treturn false;\n}\n```\n\nOther affected locations:\n- **Lines 36–43**: Add `kDfuStatusOff`, `kDfuPollTimeoutOff`, `kDfuStateOff`, `kDfuStatusOk`, and the transient DFU state constants (`kDfuStateDfuDnloadSync`, `kDfuStateDfuDnloadBusy`, `kDfuStateDfuManifestSync`, `kDfuStateDfuManifest`).\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/3e9f23d2-ae95-43fd-9a93-2